walnut trees carpet these mountains from  Horizon to Horizon this ancient forest  has grown to cover a total of thirty  thousand hectares in southern Kyrgyzstan  one that's are the main source of income  for the people who live here the nuts  are primarily brought down by young men  who climbed the trees and shake them out  of the branches there's virtually no  alternative here the trees can grow to  40 metres in height so it's a risky and  occasionally fatal business but  effective cual Nick when I'm climbing I  always try to hold a branch in one hand  with the other on another branch  obviously the higher you go the more  dangerous it gets from getting with the  nuts on the ground the whole family  comes along to pick them up they've  least the rights to the harvest from the  state the woods are swarming with people  during the walnut harvest Yogi's are  traditionally a nomadic people furniture  is rare here everyone sleeps on mats on  the ground I work with my two sons and  daughter-in-law in a good year we get  two or three tons of walnuts but this  year we've barely made 300 kilos  nonetheless the markets of Jalalabad are  still full of nuts in the shell they  cost around 2 euros a kilo but without  the shell they'll bring six euros so  pace to crack them open during the  Soviet era the entire nut harvest had to  be turned over to the state these  farmers say that's something they don't  want to go back to ever again  here in the foothills of the seven  thousand meter high tian shan mountain  range the locals face a different set of  problems though the walnut forest used  to be really dense here but there's been  a lot of deforestation new trees  urgently need to be planted but grazing  herds effectively gobble up the next  generations trees it will take 30 years  for these seedlings to grow to maturity  if there wasn't a fence here the local  livestock would soon be along to graze  yep you can see that the other side is  completely barren look at how green and  beautiful this is as nomads people here  aren't very familiar with the concept of  fences but if they can't adapt to them  Jurgis walnut could easily become very  scarce
 

